#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-imap-send(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:7
msgid "git-imap-send - Send a collection of patches from stdin to an IMAP folder"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t'git imap-send' [-v] [-q] [--[no-]curl] [(--folder|-f) <folder>]\n"
"\t'git imap-send' --list\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:24
msgid ""
"This command uploads a mailbox generated with `git format-patch` into an "
"IMAP drafts folder.  This allows patches to be sent as other email is when "
"using mail clients that cannot read mailbox files directly. The command also "
"works with any general mailbox in which emails have the fields `From`, "
"`Date`, and `Subject` in that order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:26
msgid "Typical usage is something like:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ git format-patch --signoff --stdout --attach origin | git imap-send\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-v`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--verbose`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:38
msgid "Be verbose."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-q`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--quiet`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:42
msgid "Be quiet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-f <folder>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--folder=<folder>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:47
msgid ""
"Specify the folder in which the emails have to saved.  For example: "
"`--folder=[Gmail]/Drafts` or `-f INBOX/Drafts`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--curl`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:52
msgid ""
"Use libcurl to communicate with the IMAP server, unless tunneling into it.  "
"Ignored if Git was built without the USE_CURL_FOR_IMAP_SEND option set."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-curl`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:57
msgid ""
"Talk to the IMAP server using git's own IMAP routines instead of using "
"libcurl.  Ignored if Git was built with the NO_OPENSSL option set."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--list`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:60
msgid "Run the IMAP LIST command to output a list of all the folders present."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONFIGURATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:66
msgid ""
"To use the tool, `imap.folder` and either `imap.tunnel` or `imap.host` must "
"be set to appropriate values."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "GETTING A LIST OF AVAILABLE FOLDERS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:78
msgid ""
"In order to send an email to a specific folder, you need to know the correct "
"name of intended folder in your mailbox. The names like \"Junk\", \"Trash\" "
"etc. displayed by various email clients need not be the actual names of the "
"folders stored in the mail server of your email provider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:82
msgid ""
"In order to get the correct folder name to be used with `git imap-send`, you "
"can run `git imap-send --list`. This will display a list of valid folder "
"names. An example of such an output when run on a Gmail account is:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block .
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:93
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* LIST (\\HasNoChildren) \"/\" \"INBOX\"\n"
"* LIST (\\HasChildren \\Noselect) \"/\" \"[Gmail]\"\n"
"* LIST (\\All \\HasNoChildren) \"/\" \"[Gmail]/All Mail\"\n"
"* LIST (\\Drafts \\HasNoChildren) \"/\" \"[Gmail]/Drafts\"\n"
"* LIST (\\HasNoChildren \\Important) \"/\" \"[Gmail]/Important\"\n"
"* LIST (\\HasNoChildren \\Sent) \"/\" \"[Gmail]/Sent Mail\"\n"
"* LIST (\\HasNoChildren \\Junk) \"/\" \"[Gmail]/Spam\"\n"
"* LIST (\\Flagged \\HasNoChildren) \"/\" \"[Gmail]/Starred\"\n"
"* LIST (\\HasNoChildren \\Trash) \"/\" \"[Gmail]/Trash\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:98
msgid ""
"Here, you can observe that the correct name for the \"Junk\" folder is "
"`[Gmail]/Spam` and for the \"Trash\" folder is `[Gmail]/Trash`. Similar "
"logic can be used to determine other folders as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:102
msgid "Using tunnel mode:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block .
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:107
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[imap]\n"
"    folder = \"INBOX.Drafts\"\n"
"    tunnel = \"ssh -q -C user@example.com /usr/bin/imapd ./Maildir 2> "
"/dev/null\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:110
msgid "Using direct mode:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block .
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:117
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[imap]\n"
"    folder = \"INBOX.Drafts\"\n"
"    host = imap://imap.example.com\n"
"    user = bob\n"
"    pass = p4ssw0rd\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:120
msgid "Using direct mode with SSL:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block .
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:129
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[imap]\n"
"    folder = \"INBOX.Drafts\"\n"
"    host = imaps://imap.example.com\n"
"    user = bob\n"
"    pass = p4ssw0rd\n"
"    port = 123\n"
"    ; sslVerify = false\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:138
msgid ""
"You may want to use `sslVerify=false` while troubleshooting, if you suspect "
"that the reason you are having trouble connecting is because the certificate "
"you use at the private server `example.com` you are trying to set up (or "
"have set up) may not be verified correctly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:140
msgid "Using Gmail's IMAP interface:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:147
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[imap]\n"
"    folder = \"[Gmail]/Drafts\"\n"
"    host = imaps://imap.gmail.com\n"
"    user = user@gmail.com\n"
"    port = 993\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:154
msgid ""
"Gmail does not allow using your regular password for `git imap-send`.  If "
"you have multi-factor authentication set up on your Gmail account, you can "
"generate an app-specific password for use with `git imap-send`.  Visit "
"https://security.google.com/settings/security/apppasswords to create "
"it. Alternatively, use OAuth2.0 authentication as described below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:159
msgid ""
"You might need to instead use: `folder = \"[Google Mail]/Drafts\"` if you "
"get an error that the \"Folder doesn't exist\". You can also run `git "
"imap-send --list` to get a list of available folders."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:163
msgid ""
"If your Gmail account is set to another language than English, the name of "
"the \"Drafts\" folder will be localized."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:169
msgid ""
"If you want to use OAuth2.0 based authentication, you can specify "
"`OAUTHBEARER` or `XOAUTH2` mechanism in your config. It is more secure than "
"using app-specific passwords, and also does not enforce the need of having "
"multi-factor authentication. You will have to use an OAuth2.0 access token "
"in place of your password when using this authentication."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:177
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[imap]\n"
"    folder = \"[Gmail]/Drafts\"\n"
"    host = imaps://imap.gmail.com\n"
"    user = user@gmail.com\n"
"    port = 993\n"
"    authmethod = OAUTHBEARER\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:180
msgid "Using Outlook's IMAP interface:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:183
msgid ""
"Unlike Gmail, Outlook only supports OAuth2.0 based authentication. Also, it "
"supports only `XOAUTH2` as the mechanism."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:191
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[imap]\n"
"    folder = \"Drafts\"\n"
"    host = imaps://outlook.office365.com\n"
"    user = user@outlook.com\n"
"    port = 993\n"
"    authmethod = XOAUTH2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:194
msgid "Once the commits are ready to be sent, run the following command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:196
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $ git format-patch --cover-letter -M --stdout origin/master | git "
"imap-send\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:200
msgid ""
"Just make sure to disable line wrapping in the email client (Gmail's web "
"interface will wrap lines no matter what, so you need to use a real IMAP "
"client)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:204
msgid ""
"In case you are using OAuth2.0 authentication, it is easier to use "
"credential helpers to generate tokens. Credential helpers suggested in "
"linkgit:git-send-email[1] can be used for `git imap-send` as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:206
#, no-wrap
msgid "CAUTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:213
msgid ""
"It is still your responsibility to make sure that the email message sent by "
"your email program meets the standards of your project.  Many projects do "
"not like patches to be attached.  Some mail agents will transform patches "
"(e.g. wrap lines, send them as format=flowed) in ways that make them fail.  "
"You will get angry flames ridiculing you if you don't check this."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-imap-send.adoc:217
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thunderbird in particular is known to be problematic.  Thunderbird\n"
"users may wish to visit this web page for more information:\n"
"  "
"https://kb.mozillazine.org/Plain_text_e-mail_-_Thunderbird#Completely_plain_email\n"
msgstr ""

